        <section id="uses" class="scroll-mt-28 space-y-4">
            <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold text-bone sm:text-3xl">3. How we use information</h2>
            <p>We use information to deliver software development, design, digital marketing and related agency services; plan and manage client projects; build, operate and improve our digital products; create and manage accounts; provide support; communicate with clients and users; analyze performance; market our services where permitted; secure our systems; prevent fraud; maintain business records; and comply with law. Where a product includes invoices, payment requests or checkout features, we also use relevant information to support those functions and address refunds or disputes.</p>
            <p>Depending on where you live or where processing takes place, applicable laws may include the Nigeria Data Protection Act 2023, United States federal and state privacy laws, and other local privacy or data-protection laws. We rely on appropriate legal grounds where required, such as performing a contract, complying with law, protecting legitimate business and security interests, or your consent. You can withdraw consent for future optional processing.</p>
        </section>

        <section id="payments" class="scroll-mt-28 space-y-4">
            <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold text-bone sm:text-3xl">4. Payment information</h2>
            <p>Payments are processed by independent providers such as Flutterwave, Stripe and other payment partners. When their secure checkout fields are used, full card numbers and CVCs are sent directly to the payment provider and are not intentionally stored by Techibytes.</p>
            <p>We may receive limited transaction details such as card brand, last four digits, payment token, provider reference, status, authentication result, risk result, refund and dispute information. This helps us display transaction history, provide support and address fraud or payment questions.</p>
            <p>Payment providers may use automated fraud tools that approve, decline or request extra authentication. If you believe a decision is incorrect, contact us and your payment provider or bank.</p>
        </section>

        <section id="sharing" class="scroll-mt-28 space-y-4">
            <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold text-bone sm:text-3xl">5. When we share information</h2>
            <p>We share information only as reasonably needed with clients and their authorized project teams; users and other people you ask us to work with; hosting, cloud, software-development, collaboration, communications, email, analytics, marketing, customer-support and security providers; professional advisers; and authorities when required by law.</p>
            <p>When a digital product includes payment features, we may also share relevant transaction information with merchants and customers, Flutterwave, Stripe and other payment providers, banks, card networks, and fraud or identity-verification services.</p>
            <p>Because Techibytes operates in Nigeria and the United States and uses international providers, information may be processed in those countries and other provider locations. We use reasonable contractual and security safeguards for international transfers where required.</p>
            <p>We do not sell personal information for money.</p>
        </section>

